tal cost is $$7.43.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445319 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445308 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445319 #edb/ref 1069 "q-166775" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445319 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445319 #edb/ref 1071 "Carmen has a piece of fabric with a length of $5\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{m}.$ She accidentally spills coffee on this piece, so she decides to cut out and discard $1\\,\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{m}$ of fabric. How long is the remaining piece of fabric? Express your answer as a **mixed number** in simplest form.\n\nThe remaining piece of fabric has a length of\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445319 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "86788b5f-c043-547d-a152-64c87d27af72" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445319 #edb/ref 1074 "The new piece of fabric has a length of $(5\\,\\frac{1}{4}-1\\,\\frac{1}{5})\\text{m}$ long.\n\nTo subtract two mixed numbers, we subtract whole numbers from whole numbers and fractions from fractions.\n\nSubtracting the whole numbers, we get $5-1=4.$ \n\nNow we subtract the fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nLet's look at the denominators. The least common denominator of $4$ and $5$ is $20.$\n\nTo put $\\frac{1}{4}$ over a denominator of $20,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1\\times 5}{4\\times 5}=\\frac{5}{20}\n$$\n\nTo put $\\frac{1}{5}$ over a denominator of $20,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{1\\times 4}{5\\times 4}=\\frac{4}{20}\n$$\n\nWe can now subtract the fractions. We keep the denominator the same, and we subtract the numerators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{5}{20}-\\frac{4}{20}=\\frac{1}{20}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n5\\,\\frac{1}{4}-1\\,\\frac{1}{5}=4\\,\\frac{1}{20}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445320 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445320 #edb/ref 1069 "q-166770" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445320 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445320 #edb/ref 1071 "Monica bought $10\\,\\text{m}$ of cotton fabric and paid $$39.50.$ What is the price per meter of cotton fabric?\n\nExpressed as a **decimal number**, a meter of cotton fabric costs $ \n{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445320 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "95a90288-1c66-51f3-8327-26709f04b266" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445320 #edb/ref 1074 "The meter of cotton fabric costs $$(39.50÷10).$\n\nTo perform this division, all we need to do is move the decimal point one place to the left:\n\n$$\n39.50\\to 3.950=3.95\n$$\n\nTherefore, $39.50÷10=3.95.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445321 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445321 #edb/ref 1069 "q-166774" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445321 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445321 #edb/ref 1071 "Carmen cuts two pieces of drill fabric with lengths of $\\frac{5}{6}\\,\\text{m}$ and $\\frac{9}{7}\\,\\text{m}.$ The sum of the lengths of the two pieces of fabric is{{field-1}}$\\text{m}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445321 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d13eae43-32e2-575a-85c2-71abf6bbd783" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445321 #edb/ref 1074 "The sum of the lengths of the two pieces of fabric is $(\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{9}{7})\\text{m}.$\n\nTo add two fractions with unlike denominators, we need to express each fraction as an equivalent fraction with a common denominator.\n\nLet's look at the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{6}+\\frac{9}{7}\n$$\n\nThe least common denominator of $6$ and $7$ is $42.$\n\nTo put $\\frac{5}{6}$ over a denominator of $42,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{5\\times 7}{6\\times 7}=\\frac{35}{42}\n$$\n\nTo put $\\frac{9}{7}$ over a denominator of $42,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{7}=\\frac{9\\times 6}{7\\times 6}=\\frac{54}{42}\n$$\n\nWe can now add the fractions. We keep the denominator the same, and we add the numerators.\n\n$$\n\\frac{35}{42}+\\frac{54}{42}=\\frac{89}{42}\n$$\n\nExpressing this fraction as a mixed number, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{89}{42}=2\\,\\frac{5}{42}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the lengths of the two pieces of fabric is $2\\,\\frac{5}{42}\\,\\text{m}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445322 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445307 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445322 #edb/ref 1069 "q-166773" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445322 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445322 #edb/ref 1071 "Carmen cuts a piece of drill fabric with a length of $2\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{m}$ to make a tablecloth. If the fabric has a width of $1\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{m},$ what will be the area of the tablecloth? Express your answer as a **mixed number** in simplest form.\n\nThe tablecloth will have an area of\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m}}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445322 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e72e7ec5-9f77-5705-95ed-eadc3761bae8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445322 #edb/ref 1074 "The tablecloth will have an area of $(2\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\times 1\\,\\frac{1}{2}){\\text{m}}^{2}.$\n\nFirst, we write $2\\,\\frac{1}{4}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{(2\\times 4)+1}{4}=\\frac{9}{4}\n$$\n\nWe also write $1\\,\\frac{1}{2}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{(1\\times 2)+1}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{4}\\times \\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{9\\times 3}{4\\times 2}=\\frac{27}{8}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{27}{8}=3\\,\\text{R}3=3\\,\\frac{3}{8}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445323 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "119b0ff0-218b-5f1e-9e69-3c7e87742c0b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445323 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186445314 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445324 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "318a93bb-aab6-5b65-8bfa-538cbcc6cd3c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445324 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186445319 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445325 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186445324 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445325 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "50c3a137-4d94-52b4-89d4-6b6356bc224a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445325 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186445321 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445326 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186445327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445326 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "589511b7-0670-5b54-986c-f2be952afaeb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445326 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186445318 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445327 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186445329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445327 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a35324a4-a1b7-5b6d-8c10-28e06c42be8f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445327 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186445316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445328 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186445326 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445328 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d15708ef-cb23-5891-a11f-5eaa2241a771" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445328 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186445320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445329 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186445325 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445329 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d75c4c3b-0310-5bdf-b879-77ce82b6faef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445329 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186445322 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445330 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186445328 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445330 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f03e0c40-904e-5370-ae2b-e7895a0cd2d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445330 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186445317 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
